   "source": [
    "# RoadSafe Delhi — Linear Regression Model Development (Baseline)\n",
    "## Assigned Member: Anushree\n",
    "### Task: Continuous Road Crash Density Estimation & OLS Baseline\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Project Introduction & Assigned Member\n",
    "- **Project:** RoadSafe Delhi — Explainable Road Risk Mapping and Safety Intervention Prioritization Using Machine Learning\n",
    "- **Assigned Member:** Anushree\n",
    "- **Model Assignment:** Linear Regression (`sklearn.linear_model.LinearRegression` / `Ridge`)\n",
    "- **Role:** Continuous baseline regression modeling, feature engineering support, and existing-work domain research (5 papers).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f92d6578",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Problem Statement & Model Objective\n",
    "The objective is to establish an interpretable Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) / Ridge baseline to predict continuous road risk density (`crash_density_per_km`).\n",
    "- **Strict Requirement:** Linear Regression must predict a defensible **continuous** target rather than being forced into binary classification.\n",
    "- **Target Formulation:**\n",
    "  $$\\text{crash\\_density\\_per\\_km} = \\frac{\\text{crash\\_count}}{\\text{length\\_km}}$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b36ca844",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Dataset Loading from Common Approved Dataset\n",
    "Loading the shared spatial partitions from `data_final/`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "37802592",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded Train: 11,502, Val: 4,229, Test: 3,686\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression, Ridge\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_error, r2_score\n",
    "\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \"../../..\")) if os.path.basename(os.getcwd()) == \"notebooks\" else os.path.abspath(\".\")\n",
    "DATA_FINAL_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"data_final\")\n",
    "ARTIFACTS_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"models\", \"linear_regression\", \"artifacts\")\n",
    "OUTPUTS_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"models\", \"linear_regression\", \"outputs\")\n",
    "os.makedirs(ARTIFACTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs(OUTPUTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_train = pd.read_parquet(os.path.join(DATA_FINAL_DIR, \"train.parquet\"))\n",
    "df_val = pd.read_parquet(os.path.join(DATA_FINAL_DIR, \"validation.parquet\"))\n",
    "df_test = pd.read_parquet(os.path.join(DATA_FINAL_DIR, \"test.parquet\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded Train: {len(df_train):,}, Val: {len(df_val):,}, Test: {len(df_test):,}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d90021a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Target Variable Selection (Continuous Risk Rate)\n",
    "Selected Continuous Target: `crash_density_per_km`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "40edd00e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Target: crash_density_per_km\n",
      "Train Mean Crash Density: 0.2238 crashes/km\n",
      "Val Mean Crash Density:   0.2353 crashes/km\n",
      "Test Mean Crash Density:  0.1834 crashes/km\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "target_col = \"crash_density_per_km\"\n",
    "print(f\"Target: {target_col}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Train Mean Crash Density: {df_train[target_col].mean():.4f} crashes/km\")\n",
    "print(f\"Val Mean Crash Density:   {df_val[target_col].mean():.4f} crashes/km\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Mean Crash Density:  {df_test[target_col].mean():.4f} crashes/km\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c348901b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Approved Feature Selection\n",
    "Loading `feature_contract.json` and asserting that zero outcome-derived variables enter features.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "ebb84c8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Approved Predictors: ['length_m', 'est_lanes', 'is_oneway', 'is_bridge', 'has_maxspeed', 'dist_to_center_km', 'elevation_m', 'slope_deg', 'builtup_pct', 'type']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "with open(os.path.join(DATA_FINAL_DIR, \"feature_contract.json\"), \"r\") as f:\n",
    "    contract = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "num_features = contract[\"approved_numerical_predictors\"]\n",
    "cat_features = contract[\"approved_categorical_predictors\"]\n",
    "approved_predictors = num_features + cat_features\n",
    "\n",
    "forbidden = set(contract[\"quarantined_leakage_columns\"]).union(set(contract[\"target_definitions\"].keys()))\n",
    "assert len(set(approved_predictors).intersection(forbidden)) == 0, \"FATAL: Leakage detected!\"\n",
    "print(\"Approved Predictors:\", approved_predictors)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "75c0062a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Data Preprocessing (Standard Scaling & One-Hot Encoding)\n",
    "Fitting transformations strictly on the training partition.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "0d2496cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Prepared 23 features for Linear Regression.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "scaler.fit(df_train[num_features])\n",
    "\n",
    "encoder = OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False)\n",
    "encoder.fit(df_train[cat_features])\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train = np.hstack([scaler.transform(df_train[num_features]), encoder.transform(df_train[cat_features])])\n",
    "X_val = np.hstack([scaler.transform(df_val[num_features]), encoder.transform(df_val[cat_features])])\n",
    "X_test = np.hstack([scaler.transform(df_test[num_features]), encoder.transform(df_test[cat_features])])\n",
    "\n",
    "y_train = df_train[target_col].values\n",
    "y_val = df_val[target_col].values\n",
    "y_test = df_test[target_col].values\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_names = num_features + encoder.get_feature_names_out(cat_features).tolist()\n",
    "print(f\"Prepared {X_train.shape[1]} features for Linear Regression.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ae538b8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Train-Validation-Test Data Verification (Common Spatial Split)\n",
    "Verifying disjoint spatial block boundaries.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "3d87b09d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Spatial Independence Confirmed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "assert set(df_train['spatial_block']).isdisjoint(set(df_val['spatial_block']))\n",
    "assert set(df_train['spatial_block']).isdisjoint(set(df_test['spatial_block']))\n",
    "print(\"Spatial Independence Confirmed.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "129f4895",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Model Architecture & Configuration\n",
    "Configuring regularized Ridge Linear Regression to prevent numerical collinearity instability.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "3e9323b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Configured Linear Model: Ridge(alpha=10.0, random_state=42)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "lr_model = Ridge(alpha=10.0, random_state=42)\n",
    "print(\"Configured Linear Model:\", lr_model)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "420db89b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Model Training\n",
    "Fitting linear model on `X_train`, `y_train`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "8ee6027f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Linear Regression Model Fitted.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "lr_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(\"Linear Regression Model Fitted.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f43e7fa4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Validation Tuning\n",
    "Assessing alpha regularization parameter on validation set.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "2b389555",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Validation MAE:  0.2448\n",
      "Validation RMSE: 1.3644\n",
      "Validation R²:   0.4251\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "y_val_pred = lr_model.predict(X_val)\n",
    "val_mse = mean_squared_error(y_val, y_val_pred)\n",
    "val_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_val, y_val_pred)\n",
    "val_r2 = r2_score(y_val, y_val_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Validation MAE:  {val_mae:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation RMSE: {np.sqrt(val_mse):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation R²:   {val_r2:.4f}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "79a88e32",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Final Testing on the Untouched Test Dataset\n",
    "Evaluating OLS / Ridge baseline on the untouched test partition.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "e24b4b4d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Test MAE:  0.2158 crashes/km\n",
      "Test RMSE: 1.4070 crashes/km\n",
      "Test R²:   0.3433\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "y_test_pred = lr_model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "test_mse = mean_squared_error(y_test, y_test_pred)\n",
    "test_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test, y_test_pred)\n",
    "test_r2 = r2_score(y_test, y_test_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Test MAE:  {test_mae:.4f} crashes/km\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test RMSE: {np.sqrt(test_mse):.4f} crashes/km\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test R²:   {test_r2:.4f}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99d976e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Evaluation Metrics & Visualizations\n",
    "Plotting Regression Coefficients and Residual Distribution.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "f40af31e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "coefs = pd.Series(lr_model.coef_, index=feature_names).sort_values()\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "coefs.plot(kind=\"barh\", color=\"#2980b9\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Ridge Linear Regression Coefficients (Crash Density / km)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Coefficient Weight\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUTPUTS_DIR, \"coefficients.png\"), dpi=200)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Residuals Plot\n",
    "residuals = y_test - y_test_pred\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "sns.histplot(residuals.clip(-5, 5), bins=40, kde=True, color=\"#8e44ad\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Residual Error Distribution (Clipped at ±5 crashes/km)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"True - Predicted\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(os.path.join(OUTPUTS_DIR, \"residuals_distribution.png\"), dpi=200)\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c066f31f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
